  "title": "AMR: Fix fallback to bandwidth-efficient mode",
  "description": "The AMR dissector, when set to decode as octet aligned, has an\nexpert info if the four reserved bits are nonzero, which claims\nthat it will fall back to dissecting as bandwidth-efficient.\n(This auto-detects bandwidth-efficient mode except when the AMR\nmode is 0 or 1.)\n\nHowever, it doesn't actually do the fallback. Do so.\n\nRelated to #17608",
